   "line": [
    "Nxc3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Recapture the pawn with the knight — the tempting central push has a drawback while the bishop sits on c4, because a counter-thrust to d5 hits that bishop and frees the defender's game. Once the knight recaptures, that push becomes a genuine threat of your own.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 101,
   "fen": "rnbqk2r/pppp1ppp/5n2/8/1bB1P3/2N5/PP3PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [
    "Bb4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The entire point of the gambit is a lead in development, and it demands speed — let the opponent castle and consolidate and you're simply a pawn down for nothing. Step on the gas before the king finds shelter.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 115.5,
