   "line": [
    "Kxe7"
   ],
   "spoken": "A nice concrete question — castle short or long? The answer is long. It may look risky with the queenside pawns gone, but with the queens off and the opponent undeveloped the king is in zero danger, and castling long automatically springs the rook into the game. Far more efficient than a slow rook move.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 28,
   "t": 597,
   "fen": "r1b4r/ppp1kppp/5n2/3B4/8/5N2/P2B1PPP/2KR3R w - - 2 15",
   "line": [
