    "d5"
   ],
   "spoken": "For the theory record, the traditional way to equalise against the Danish is the central break d5, handing a pawn back to accelerate development. It's the safest, most reliable route to a level game.",
   "kind": "plan",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 782.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/ppp2ppp/8/3B4/4P3/8/PB3PPP/RN1QK1NR b KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "Bxd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "After that break, recapture with the bishop, not the pawn — taking with the pawn would leave the bishop looking foolish. Grabbing with the bishop opens a diagonal against it and lands it awkwardly, so the knight develops with tempo, gaining time on the opponent's main attacking piece.",
   "kind": "plan",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
